Copyright 2024-2025 Bytedance Ltd. and/or its affiliates and the verl contributors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Original copyright and license
headers are retained in the files under verl/. Modifications for GraphDancer
include the multi-turn graph-agent rollout hook, the format-aware rule-based
reward, the graph-aware curriculum sampler (verl/experimental/dataset/crl_e2h.py),
per-question evaluation output, and checkpoint-retention safeguards. Some trainers
and advantage estimators that GraphDancer does not use were removed; GraphDancer
uses the PPO (GAE) path.

verl in turn contains code derived from third-party projects (e.g. Hugging Face
Transformers, vLLM, SGLang, PyTorch, Megatron-LM); see the headers of the
respective files.

The multi-turn rollout loop and the exact-match reward follow the design of
Search-R1 (https://github.com/PeterGriffinJin/Search-R1, Apache License 2.0).

The graph environments, graph functions (RetrieveNode, NodeFeature,
NeighbourCheck, NodeDegree), the GRBench questions, the in-context
demonstrations embedded in data/split701020_v1/prompt_templates.json, and the
GPTScore judge prompt come from Graph-CoT / GRBench
(https://github.com/PeterGriffinJin/Graph-CoT). The GRBench data are not
redistributed here except for question identifiers, frozen labels and prompt
templates; obtain the data from the original release and follow its terms.
